# notes/px122/rig/ab.manifest — one commit's timing take (take.sh): CI's mpx3-shell steps "the shell
# runs programs" (every leg) and "the same typing rows with the xHCI on MSI only, then INTx only"
# (the all tier's), every boot TCG as on the runners, then the rows' time per leg and the kernel's
# own boot lines. Taken at the last green trunk and at the first trunk whose runs were cancelled.
# The two timed steps need nothing of each other's verdict: the local Linux side has no container
# engine for its as-a-user sessions and lists `ls -l` totals of the container's own file system, so
# those rows are red here whatever the kernel does; their boots still run and are timed.
floor 35
rig lib.sh committed=../../..:HEAD:notes/px122/rig/lib.sh
rig stamped.py committed=../../..:HEAD:notes/px122/rig/stamped.py
rig ab.manifest committed=../../..:HEAD:notes/px122/rig/ab.manifest
step suite image=localhost/px75-ubuntu:2 tools=cc,clang,readelf,python3,git,curl,qemu-system-x86_64,xorriso script=step.sh -- suite
step irq image=localhost/px75-ubuntu:2 tools=qemu-system-x86_64,python3 script=step.sh -- irq
step times tools=python3 script=step.sh -- times
